# Supply chain

## Dependencies

- Commit the lockfile the ecosystem uses. Review the new packages in a
  dependency change, not only the direct name in the manifest
- Prefer a well-known, maintained package over a new transitive chain for the
  same job
- Pin production base images and remote installers to a version or digest.
  Do not track a floating `latest` tag for a production artifact
- Do not pipe a remote script into a shell in a build unless the URL is pinned
  and the project already accepts that pattern
- Read install scripts of a newly added package when they run code at install
  time

## CI and build

- CI secrets come from the platform secret store. Do not echo them in logs
- Do not grant a build job permission to push, deploy, or read production
  secrets unless that job's purpose is that action
- Do not claim a vulnerability scan passed unless this turn ran the scanner
  and read its result
